   "text": {
    "L1": "A rectangle has four right angles, and its opposite sides are equal.",
    "L2": "Four equal sides alone do not guarantee a square. The angles must also be 90 degrees.",
    "L3": "First, draw PQ as 5 centimetres with a ruler.",
    "L4": "Make a right angle at P and another right angle at Q.",
    "L5": "Open the compass to 3 centimetres. Mark S from P and R from Q on the perpendicular lines.",
    "L6": "Join S to R. Check that SR is 5 centimetres and every corner is 90 degrees.",
    "L7": "So the construction uses both side lengths and right angles. Now choose the first step."
   },
